{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"grassy-cracked-morpho","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe completed fix on reportable-chalkstony-eeve skips full-history commit discovery only when accepted-scope file impact is empty. Impact-present closes still run the same unbounded path, and current end-to-end telemetry shows it now dominates the user-visible close command.\n\nFrozen Codex-rollout sample (2026-08-22 through 2026-08-23T21:15Z), limited to canonical tracker closes with a matched Bedrock COMPLETION_VERDICT and metrics.llm_calls > 0: n=10 completed closes, p50=28.24m, p90=57.32m, p99=61.60m. The matched completion-verifier workflows themselves are generally 1-4m; recent 25-62m closes spend most of their time before the verifier sidecar.\n\nStatic mechanism: close_precheck._check_work_landed calls commit_impact.referencing_commits for every impact-present close. That helper reads all 2,690 commits and extract_ticket_refs produces 2,229 unique historical candidates. 702 candidates require alias/prefix resolution; _scan_alias walks the current 5,351-ticket store for each, implying roughly 3.8 million ticket-directory visits before completion verification. Ordinary subject prefixes and deprecated four-digit references enter the candidate set. This is the residual impact-present case left explicitly unchanged by reportable-chalkstony-eeve.\n\n## Plan\n- Add a deterministic performance reproduction for an impact-present close with many historical reference candidates and a large tracker.\n- Replace per-candidate full-store alias resolution with a batch/indexed resolution strategy while preserving every accepted commit-ticket reference form and ambiguity behavior.\n- Keep descendant credit, attached commits, --ref behavior, file-impact-vs-diff enforcement, and fail-closed git-error semantics unchanged.\n- Measure the repaired pre-verifier scan and pin a scaling assertion that prevents history x tracker behavior from returning.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Impact-present close commit discovery does not perform a full tracker walk per unique historical candidate.\n- [ ] The scan cost is bounded to one tracker index/build per invocation plus linear code-history parsing.\n- [ ] Full, two-quad short, alias, Jira, compatibility four-digit/prefix, trailer, and leading-subject reference forms retain current matching and ambiguity semantics.\n- [ ] Descendant ticket credit and file-impact-vs-diff enforcement remain covered end to end.\n- [ ] A scale-focused regression test fails on the current history-times-tracker implementation and passes on the repair.\n- [ ] Before/after wall-time and scan-count evidence is recorded on this ticket.","id":"a8ac-48b5-0759-40e5","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["performance","completion-gate","discovered"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Impact-present ticket close scales with code history times tracker size"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787525881223169001,"uuid":"96b90c15-c494-4519-bf2a-92f5bf02a06f"}